Patch 6004: cellFsRead records the time of the last read (g_ppu_fs_last_read_ms).

Steady-clock milliseconds of the last cellFsRead, so a host can wait until file streaming goes quiet. The J-Stars
host holds its game-data check until then (jsp_hle.cpp game_data_check), the same fix as the v0.15 port: without it
the CPK re-bind after the check lands mid-way through the boot-logo stream, and the boot stays on "Now loading" or
the skipped block corrupts memory. No behaviour change on its own.

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp b/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
index 37e37454..23544682 100644
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_fs.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,11 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <chrono>
+
+/* Steady-clock milliseconds of the last cellFsRead, for a host that waits until file
+ * streaming goes quiet (J-Stars holds its game-data check until then). */
+extern "C" { volatile unsigned long long g_ppu_fs_last_read_ms = 0; }
 #include <mutex>
 #include <atomic>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
@@ -526,6 +531,8 @@ static void cellFsRead(ppu_context* ctx)
      * the end of the log and look identical to reads that never happen.
      * FS_READ_ALL=1 logs every read; otherwise a per-fd first-read line plus a
      * periodic summary is enough to tell the two apart. */
+    g_ppu_fs_last_read_ms = (unsigned long long)std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(
+        std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();
     { static uint64_t tot=0; static int _n=0;
       static uint64_t per_fd[64]; static uint32_t cnt_fd[64];
       tot+=n;
